 rounds to `2.68`.\n\nCI: passed (run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 380189, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_019rDsMQQUzYudKeGahrxy4b", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 380189, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019rDsMQQUzYudKeGahrxy4b", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 385858, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own description says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212).\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **Result:** 2.665 now rounds to 2.66 instead of 2.67. 2.675 still rounds to 2.68.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nFIN-212 isn't in the security advisory system, so it's probably an internal ticket. I relied on the code's description and the test, which both say to use banker's rounding.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0118Hcd3j5dPdS2NSfS54kae", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_n